// prototype-default-merging.  A function REACHED from the SELECTED ENTRY may not carry a
// RETURN semantic.  MEASURED against the established compiler - the C5122 diagnostic's own
// text ("semantics not allowed on functions other than the entry function") is
// WRONG about its rule: the established compiler accepts a parameter semantic on a called
// helper, and accepts full semantics on a function nothing calls.
//
// PARAMETER semantic on a called helper - the diagnostic text
// forbids this and the established compiler ACCEPTS it
// Compile with -e beta.  Reference verdict: ACCEPT
float4 alpha(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) { return t*2.0; }
float4 beta(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return alpha(t)*0.5; }
